--- NOTED DECISIONS (no silent drift) ---
* SI preserved end-to-end: repository caches the RAW server JsonElement verbatim; derivations never coerce
  numeric-kind null values to 0 (golden: adaptObservationsSteersValueByKind row[4]). Unit conversion stays
  display-only (S5), never in this layer.
* Response-shape source-of-truth = the Go backend JSON (snake_case), matching established S8 siblings
  (Signals/FleetTelemetry). The web `@/types/telemetry` SignalHistoryResponse `{timestamp,valueNum}` shape is
  STALE/nominal; the real /signals/{id}/{sig}/history endpoint (internal/api/signalinspect/handler.go) emits the
  typed `{ts,kind,value}` point, so SignalHistoryPoint was modeled as {ts,kind,value:JsonElement?}.
* TTL mapping mirrors web staleTime via constants.ts STALE_TIMES: live-signals + observations = REALTIME 5s;
  catalog = SLOW 5min; all others = STANDARD 60s. CacheDomain.Telemetry default = 1.minutes.
* useSignalCatalog is deprecated/404 on the backend (per web hook comment) — ported faithfully (returns the same
  empty/erroring shape) without inventing a new endpoint.
* Mutation invalidation mirrors web invalidateQueries via prefix-match family keys (separator "|"); error-vins and
  errors families have disjoint first segments (TanStack array-prefix semantics) so they never cross-invalidate.

